# {{ component.name }}

A general Python package with importable code and an execution entrypoint. There is no framework, HTTP server or
business behavior yet. Use it for actual automation, worker, service, robotics or reusable-code requirements.

## Code and responsibilities

- `src/{{ component.module }}/__init__.py`: importable scaffold; importing does not start connections/tasks or alter the environment.
- `src/{{ component.module }}/__main__.py`: calls `main()` only through `python -m {{ component.module }}`.
  The current entrypoint exits without external effects; importing the package/entrypoint does not execute it.
- `tests/test_smoke.py`: installed-package import smoke, not product regression coverage.
- `pyproject.toml`: distribution name, supported Python range, build backend and development dependencies.

Split responsibilities when real inputs, use cases or I/O appear. Select an HTTP framework profile when HTTP is needed;
do not pre-create `domain/`, `application/`, `adapters/` or abstract base classes.
Do not hide expected failures behind successful defaults. Composition or the creating object owns mutable state and
external resources, including partial-startup cleanup. Read secrets at configuration boundaries; avoid import-time
configuration reads and I/O.

## Environment and checks

This component owns `pyproject.toml`, `.venv/` and its generated `uv.lock`. If adopting a parent Python workspace, define
shared environment/lock ownership too. Separate installation/lock creation from verification.

```sh
uv sync --dev
uv run --locked pytest
uv build
```

After installation, run the entrypoint with:

```sh
uv run --locked python -m {{ component.module }}
```

It currently exits without I/O and starts no server. The manifest supports Python 3.10 or later. Pins checked against
PyPI metadata on 2026-10-26 are [hatchling 1.32.4](https://pypi.org/pypi/hatchling/1.32.4/json) and
[pytest 9.1.1](https://pypi.org/pypi/pytest/9.1.1/json). Review supported versions and locks when changing them.
Generated tests cover packaging/import smoke only; add behavior tests with the actual implementation.

